  "final_message": "Trace of `service.checkout(\"7781\")`:\n\n1. `service.py:6` \u2014 `checkout` calls `write_audit(\"order\", order_id)` with `order_id = \"7781\"`.\n2. `audit.py:9-12` \u2014 `write_audit` builds the key via `_format_key(kind, ident)` and sets `log[key] = True`.\n3. `audit.py:5-6` \u2014 `_format_key` returns `f\"{AUDIT_PREFIX}-{kind.upper()}-{ident}\"`.\n4. `config.py:3` \u2014 `AUDIT_PREFIX = \"AUD\"`.\n\nSo the key is `\"AUD\"` + `\"-\"` + `\"ORDER\"` + `\"-\"` + `\"7781\"`. Executing the code confirms the audit log dict ends up as `{'AUD-ORDER-7781': True}`.\n\nThe decoy modules are irrelevant: `decoy_metrics.py` uses `METRICS_PREFIX = \"MET\"` and writes to a separate metrics dict, and `decoy_cache.py` never touches the audit log. Neither is called from `checkout`.\n\nANSWER: AUD-ORDER-7781",
